<title>UK: Euromarket turnover rose in week to Apr 17 - ISMA.</title>
<headline>Euromarket turnover rose in week to Apr 17 - ISMA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turnover in Eurobond and related markets rose to $932.08 billion in the week to April 17 from $911.11 billion the previous week, International Securities Market Association data showed (in billions of dollars):</p>
<p>					  Latest week	Previous week</p>
<p> Primary market:		     51.00		50.16</p>
<p> Of which U.S. dollar issues     25.48		20.85</p>
<p> Secondary market:		  881.08	     860.95</p>
<p> Of which U.S. dollar issues    203.37	     217.55</p>
<p> Cleared through Euroclear	688.70	     657.57</p>
<p> Cleared through Cedel	    243.38	     253.54</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
